==Russian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ru|ребёнокъ||ru-PRO}}

===Etymology===
{{root|ru|ine-pro|*h₃erbʰ-}}
{{inh+|ru|orv|робѧ}}, diminutive of {{m|orv|робъ||slave}} from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*orbę}}. Compare with {{m|ru|па́робок||lad}} {{q|dialectal}}. The relationship with "slave" could arise from the meaning "orphan" because orphans carried out the hard work in the household.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA}}
** {{audio|ru|Ru-ребёнок.ogg}}
* {{IPA|ru|[rɨˈbʲonak]|a=Belarus}} (''phonetic respelling'': рыбёнак)
* {{IPA|ru|[rʲiˈbʲɔnɐk]|a=Ukraine}} phonetic respelling: ребёнак)

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|f|реб|ёнок/ь-m|де́т|or|ребёнок|dat_pl=де́тям,ребя́там*|ins_pl=детьми́,ребя́тами*|pre_pl=де́тях,ребя́тах*|a=an|pltail=*|adj=де́тский,ребя́ческий,ребя́чий|dim=ребёночек}}

# {{qualifier|plural {{lang|ru|де́ти}}, less commonly {{lang|ru|ребя́та}}}} [[child]], [[kid]], [[baby]]: [[children]], [[kids]], [[babies]]
#: {{syn|ru|дитя́}}
# {{lb|ru|plural only}} {{qualifier|plural {{lang|ru|ребя́та}}}} [[guy]]s, [[fellow]]s, [[friend]]s, [[comrade]]s

====Usage notes====
* The singular form can only refer to "child"/"baby" sense.
* The plural form {{m|ru|ребя́та}} can mean "guys", "friends", etc.
* For the plural form "children" {{m|ru|де́ти}} is the preferred word but {{m|ru|ребя́та}} is also used.

====Declension====
{{ru-noun-table||#*/ь-m|де́т|or||gen_pl=дете́й,ребя́т*|ins_pl=детьми́,ребя́тами*|a=an|pltail=*|notes=* Use the second plural with the meaning "friends!", "fellows!", "guys!", "comrades!".}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|be|рабёнак|bor=1}}

